        but “usable” is not “current”. The sheet predates the latest Gulf premium moves, and the
        corridor context matters: Gulf-side routes have spent 2026 absorbing geopolitical premia,
        which is exactly why every figure carries its date.
      </p>
      <p>
        One pattern worth noting before you read the table: the two origin sheets sit close together.
        Shanghai and Shenzhen do not differ much per box on this lane, so the origin decision is a
        service and sailing-frequency question more than a price question. Use the bands below as
        your negotiating frame, then test the live market with an RFQ.
      </p>

